# GLM-5.3-Flash UNCENSORED, EXL3 TR3 4-bit, on TensorFold across both Sparks
# (TP 2, one rank per Spark). 320B total / 18B active, 175.7 GB of weights
# (~95.5 GB per rank). Max's pick for the Sparks, 2026-09-30: "GLM-5.3-Flash
# by orcarouter, or an EXL3 variant". All OpenBeast models are uncensored, so
# the Sparks serve this and never a stock checkpoint. Details, the memory fit
# and the alternatives are in docs/DGX_SPARK_PLAN.md ("GLM-5.3-Flash").
#
# Why this repo: it is orcarouter's abliterated GLM-5.3-Flash
# (orcarouter/GLM-5.3-Flash-Uncensored-FP8) quantized by neko-legends in the
# ShapleyMCG "TR3" layout. That is the only EXL3 layout TensorFold's
# glm5_next CUDA engine reads: quantization_config must hold exactly
#   bits 4, codebook "mcg", scope "glm53_routed_experts_only"
# (EXL3_VARIANT, families/glm5_next/__init__.py:21 @ v0.5.0 9cd52ab), with the
# experts under their plain names (cuda/weights.py:325-350). It is the
# uncensored twin of the tested Mia-AiLab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-TR3-4bpw: the Hub
# reports the SAME per-dtype element counts for both repos, to the element
# (I16 77,913,391,104 / BF16 9,669,171,456 / F16 228,261,888 / F32 295,518 /
# I32 37,152), and cbert33's lossless rank-sliced copy of it records 150,226
# source tensors, the count in Mia's index.
#
# Not usable instead:
# - weights/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-TR3-4bpw (the staged Mia / brandonmusic TR3
#   mirror) is the STOCK model — no abliteration — so it is out under the
#   uncensored rule. It stays useful only as a known-good TensorFold smoke of
#   the Sparks' plumbing; never route users to it.
# - cbert33/GLM-5.3-Flash-Uncensored-EXL3-DGX-Sliced: same weights, but each
#   routed expert is stored as experts.N.proj.rank0/rank1.trellis for its own
#   vLLM fork; TensorFold looks up experts.N.proj.trellis and cannot load it
#   (model-inspect says so).
# - MikeRoz/…-Uncensored-*bpw-h6-exl3 and turboderp's EXL3: stock exllamav3
#   "mul1" codebook, all layers quantized — TensorFold refuses them at start.
# - orcarouter's NVFP4 (205 GB) fits two Sparks only above 0.85 memory
#   utilization and needs vLLM >= v0.30.0; FP8 (328 GB) does not fit at all.
#
# VERIFY (the repo is gated — "gated: auto" — so its files could not be read
# on 2026-09-30 without accepting the licence on the Hub first):
#   1. Request access on the Hub, then with a token in a 0600 file run
#        HF_TOKEN_FILE=<file> scripts/backends/model-inspect.sh \
#          neko-legends/GLM-5.3-Flash-Uncensored-EXL3@07135ec082f8f11f7a71e4244a4e5167a0f96277
#      and confirm "tensorfold SUPPORTED … ranks: 2" — i.e. config.json's
#      quantization_config really is 4 / mcg / glm53_routed_experts_only.
#   2. Its licence is ShapleyMCG License 1.0 (attribution required), not
#      MIT: read it before redistributing anything built on it.
#   3. On hardware: both ranks load, conformance.sh passes (tool calls come
#      back as OpenAI tool_calls — TensorFold converts GLM's
#      <arg_key>/<arg_value> itself; the vLLM spelling would be the glm47
#      tool-call and reasoning parsers, which a tensorfold profile does not
#      take), and TensorFold's EXL3 path is labelled EXPERIMENTAL upstream
#      (docs/recipes/glm-5.3-flash.md: speed, capacity, long context TBD).
BACKEND=tensorfold
SOURCE=neko-legends/GLM-5.3-Flash-Uncensored-EXL3
REVISION=07135ec082f8f11f7a71e4244a4e5167a0f96277
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=glm-5.3-flash-uncensored
# The family refuses anything but --tp 2 (families/glm5_next/__init__.py:179-181).
TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=2
# Empty = the model's native 1,048,576; TensorFold sizes the KV cache from
# what is left after ~95.5 GB of weights per rank and says so at start. Set a
# number once the hardware run shows the real capacity.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=
# auto = one request at a time on CUDA.
TENSORFOLD_PARALLEL=auto
# No drafter: TensorFold's GLM drafter (incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2) is
# licensed CC BY-NC-ND, which OpenBeast has not reviewed; without one the
# engine drafts with the checkpoint's own MTP layer (VERIFY that neko's
# conversion kept it: config num_nextn_predict_layers >= 1).
